{"id":"12B","title":"Meddling and Gossip","part":{"n":12,"title":"Etiquette and moral issues"},"url":"/law/12-etiquette-and-moral-issues/12b","entries":[{"id":"12B.1","text":"Busybodies exhorted to mind their own business.","refs":[{"book":"2 Thessalonians","chapter":3,"verses":"11-12"},{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":26,"verses":"17"},{"book":"1 Peter","chapter":4,"verses":"15"}],"citation":"2 Thes. 3:11-12; Prov. 26:17; 1 Pet. 4:15."},{"id":"12B.2","text":"Christians exhorted not to suffer as a consequence of being a meddler in other people's matters.","refs":[{"book":"1 Peter","chapter":4,"verses":"15"}],"citation":"1 Pet 4:15."},{"id":"12B.3","text":"We are not to wander from house to house as tattlers and busybodies.","refs":[{"book":"1 Timothy","chapter":5,"verses":"13"}],"citation":"1 Tim. 5:13."},{"id":"12B.4","text":"We should not meddle in other's concerns.","refs":[{"book":"2 Kings","chapter":14,"verses":"10"},{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":20,"verses":"3"},{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":24,"verses":"21"},{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":26,"verses":"17"}],"citation":"2 Kings 14:10; Prov. 20:3; Prov. 24:21; Prov. 26:17."},{"id":"12B.5","text":"Gossiping is not proper and a sign of a depraved mind.","refs":[{"book":"Romans","chapter":1,"verses":"28-29"}],"citation":"Rom. 1:28-29."},{"id":"12B.6","text":"Every fool will be meddling.","refs":[{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":20,"verses":"3"}],"citation":"Prov. 20:3."},{"id":"12B.7","text":"We are admonished not to gossip.","refs":[{"book":"2 Corinthians","chapter":12,"verses":"20"}],"citation":"2 Cor. 12:20."},{"id":"12B.8","text":"We should not talk about the errors or transgressions of others.","refs":[{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":17,"verses":"9"}],"citation":"Prov. 17:9."},{"id":"12B.9","text":"Gossip often arises from hatred.","refs":[{"book":"Psalms","chapter":41,"verses":"7"}],"citation":"Psa. 41:7."},{"id":"12B.10","text":"Gossip causes a separation in friendship.","refs":[{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":16,"verses":"28"},{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":17,"verses":"9"}],"citation":"Prov. 16:28; Prov. 17:9."},{"id":"12B.11","text":"Do not associate with a gossip.","refs":[{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":20,"verses":"19"}],"citation":"Prov. 20:19."},{"id":"12B.12","text":"Where gossiping is eliminated, strife ceases.","refs":[{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":26,"verses":"20"}],"citation":"Prov. 26:20."}]}